## Workspace

Summaries can use outcome data and receipts. Do not copy message histories into the coordinator when compact findings suffice.
Keep large collections in Scheme bindings. End execute with counts, compact findings, or bounded previews, not the full saved collection.
Named Scheme bindings persist automatically. There is no store primitive; create or update a binding with define or set!.
Tool replies over 8000 bytes become {kind: preview, complete: false, truncated: true, ref, value_info, preview}.
value_info describes the full saved value; preview is only an excerpt and never proves coverage.
Use `(recall "workspace-reference")` inside Scheme, then transform or slice the value. Returning it unchanged produces another preview.
Worker results contain compact findings plus input_ref and receipts_ref; recall those references when needed.
Large worker inputs arrive as workspace references the worker can recall. Tool-free reason inputs must fit the configured model input limit.
Process large deterministic values in bounded batches. For independent semantic investigations, pass stable references to spawn-agent rather
than centralizing source evidence into reason batches. Never divide one semantic unit into incomplete excerpts.
A Scheme evaluation limit applies to one execute call, not the whole task. Continue smaller read-only batches from saved progress.
If evidence is insufficient, say so instead of inventing conclusions.
